# Copy and paste, headlessly: Ctrl-V from another pane, a cut pasted back,
# and Ctrl-A with typing over it. A replay never runs a clipboard tool; the
# `clipboard` command fills the fake one Ctrl-V reads, and a copy writes it.
# No database: scripts/qa.sh runs this with a state directory of its own,
# because it types into an empty pad.

expect ╭ Objects

# Nothing on either clipboard yet.
key Ctrl-V
expect the clipboard is empty

# Ctrl-V from Objects: the pad takes the focus and the text, which the
# Shift-Left and Ctrl-X below prove by acting on it.
key Shift-Tab
clipboard select 1
key Ctrl-V
expect 1 select 1
expect pasted 1 line

# A cut goes onto the clipboard, and pastes back twice.
key Shift-Left
key Ctrl-X
expect cut 1 character
expect-not select 1
key Ctrl-V
key Ctrl-V
expect 1 select 11

# A bracketed paste from Results lands in the pad too.
key Shift-Tab
key Shift-Tab
paste  from t
expect 1 select 11 from t

# Ctrl-C with nothing selected copies the statement.
key Ctrl-C
expect copied the statement

# Ctrl-A selects the whole pad and typing replaces it; after a pause, one
# Ctrl-Z takes both back.
wait 600
key Ctrl-A
type select 2
expect 1 select 2
expect-not select 11
key Ctrl-Z
expect 1 select 11 from t

# And the statement copied above comes back over a selection of all of it.
key Ctrl-A
key Ctrl-V
expect 1 select 11 from t
expect pasted 1 line

frame clipboard
key Ctrl-Q
